---
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import FooterScripts from '../../../components/FooterScripts.astro';
import SrkrHeader from '../../../components/SrkrHeader.astro';
import SrkrFooter from '../../../components/SrkrFooter.astro';
import OffCanvas from '../../../components/OffCanvas.astro';
import DeptNav from '../../../components/DeptNav.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="Department of Information Technology | SRKR Engineering College" description="Department of Information Technology at SRKR Engineering College, Bhimavaram — established 2001, NBA accredited, B.Tech in Information Technology." />
  </head>
  <body>
    <SrkrHeader />

    <!-- BREADCRUMB -->
    <section class="rts-breadcrumb breadcrumb-height breadcumb-bg" style="background-image: url(/assets/images/banner/breadcrumb.jpg);">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-12">
            <div class="breadcrumb-content">
              <ul class="breadcrumb">
                <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li>
                <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/departments">Departments</a></li>
                <li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Information Technology</li>
              </ul>
              <h1 class="section-title">Department of Information Technology</h1>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- BREADCRUMB AREA END -->

    <!-- content -->
    <div class="rts-faculty-details py-5">
      <div class="container">

        <DeptNav dept="it" current="Home" />

        <!-- About the Department -->
        <div class="row align-items-center justify-content-md-center mb-5 pb-5">
          <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-11">
            <div class="faculty-content-text me-5">
              <h3 class="rts-section-title mb-5">About the Department</h3>
              <p style="text-align: justify;">Established in 1999, the Department of Information Technology has grown into a vibrant center for excellence in education, research, and innovation. The department initially started with an intake of 60 students in the B.Tech (Information Technology) program, which has since expanded to 180 students. It currently offers Undergraduate (B.Tech), Postgraduate (M.Tech in Information Technology), and Ph.D. programs, catering to the evolving demands of the IT industry and academia.</p>
              <p style="text-align: justify;">The department is committed to providing quality technical education through innovative teaching-learning practices, industry-oriented training, and research-driven initiatives. Equipped with spacious classrooms, e-classrooms, a modern library, a fully air-conditioned seminar hall, and state-of-the-art computer laboratories, the department provides an excellent learning environment. High-speed internet connectivity and advanced computing facilities support students and faculty in academic, research, and development activities.</p>
              <p style="text-align: justify;">The department offers B.Tech programs in Information Technology, Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Computer Science and Business Systems, and Computer Science and Information Technology, along with a two-year M.Tech program in Information Technology. Through hands-on laboratory experience, industry collaborations, technical events, and research opportunities, students develop strong technical, analytical, and problem-solving skills. The department prepares graduates for successful careers in leading IT organizations, innovative startups, higher education, and research institutions worldwide.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-11">
            <div class="ratio ratio-16x9 mt-5 mt-lg-0">
              <iframe
                src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/zWHp1cRW8fc?html5=1&enablejsapi=1"
                title="SRKR Department Video"
                loading="lazy"
                allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
                referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
                allowfullscreen
              ></iframe>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Message from HoD -->
        <div class="row mt--30">
          <div class="rts-section mb--60">
            <h3 class="rts-section-title">Message from Head of Department</h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-8">
            <div class="faculty-image text-center">
              {/* TODO: replace with real faculty photo */}
              <img class="img-fluid mw-100" src="/assets/images/faculty/it/1356.jpg" alt="Dr.P.Ravi Kiran Varma">
              <div class="h5 mb-2 mt-5">Dr. P. Ravi Kiran Varma</div>
              <span>Professor &amp; Head of Department</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-8">
            <div class="faculty-content-text ms-lg-5 mt-5 mt-lg-0">
              <p class="h6 mb-4">Welcome to the Department of Information Technology</p>
              <p class="mb-5">Established in 1999, the Department of Information Technology at SRKR Engineering College has spent more than two decades preparing engineers for the fast-moving world of software, web, cloud and data. With a current B.Tech sanctioned intake of 180 and an NBA-accredited curriculum, our students learn to build the systems that power modern digital businesses — from full-stack web applications and mobile apps to cloud-native services and data pipelines.</p>
              <p class="h6 mb-4">A Curriculum Built for the Modern Stack</p>
              <p class="mb-5">Our programme blends timeless computing fundamentals — data structures, operating systems, databases and computer networks — with the technologies graduates are hired to use on day one: full-stack JavaScript, Python, Java, Spring Boot, REST APIs, SQL &amp; NoSQL databases, AWS / Azure cloud, Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD pipelines, mobile app development, and cyber security. Specialised electives in DevOps, Data Analytics, Machine Learning and Information Security give students the freedom to specialise as their interests evolve.</p>
              <p class="h6 mb-4">Industry Engagement, Placements &amp; Student Life</p>
              <p>Our graduates are placed every year with top recruiters including TCS, Infosys, Wipro, Cognizant, HCL, Tech Mahindra, Accenture, Amazon and Microsoft, with our highest recent offer at <strong>17.16 LPA</strong> from Amazon. Beyond placements, students learn through full-semester internships, hackathons, open-source contribution drives, and active technical societies. We warmly invite you to explore what the Department of Information Technology has to offer and look forward to welcoming you into our community.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="border-top my-60"></div>

          <!-- Mission & Vision -->
          <div class="row align-items-center justify-content-md-center">
            <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-11 rts-scholarship-description">
              <div class="faculty-content-text si__list me-5">

                <h4 class="font-32 mb-3 mt-4">Vision</h4>
                <ul class="list-unstyled one-column-list mb-0">
                  <li class="mb-3">To evolve as a centre of excellence by adopting innovative methods for teaching learning and research in the diversified fields of Information Technology.</li>
                </ul>

                <h4 class="font-32 mb-4">Mission</h4>
                <ul class="list-unstyled one-column-list">
                  <li class="mb-3">The highest quality technology-based education and services in the most effective manner.</li>
                  <li class="mb-3">Maintain a vital, state-of-art research to provide its students and faculty with opportunities to create, interpret, apply and disseminate knowledge.</li>
                  <li class="mb-3">Empower students towards higher education, research and becoming entrepreneur/employee and meet intellectual, ethical, carrier challenges and community service.</li>
                </ul>

              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-6 col-md-11">
